+// Object references are 8-byte aligned, stack locals pointer-aligned, localloc space STACK_ALIGN'ed and
+// handles (statics, string literals, frozen objects) at least pointer-aligned. Arithmetic keeps the low zero bits it can prove:
 // a sum, difference or OR has as many as the weaker operand, a shift by n adds n, a product adds both
 // operands', an AND has at least the stronger operand's (masking only clears bits) and an integral cast
 // keeps them. A local has the alignment ComputeAlignedLocals found for every value stored to it.
@@ -1315,6 +1315,10 @@
